{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q419723","formula":"CBrClF₂","hill":"CBrClF2","elements":["C","F","Cl","Br"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"F":2.0,"Br":1.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Bromochlorodifluoromethane","ru":"Бромхлордифторметан"},"descriptions":{"en":"Bromochlorodifluoromethane (BCF), also referred to by the code numbers Halon 1211 and Freon 12B1, is a haloalkane with the chemical formula CF2ClBr. It is used for fire suppression, especially for expensive equipment or items that could be damaged by the residue from other types of extinguishers. It is stored as a liquid under pressure and vaporizes when discharged to suppress fires.","ru":"Дифторхлорбромметан (R12B1) — химическое соединение, фреон с химической формулой CF2ClBr. Дифторхлорбромметан используется для тушения пожаров, особенно для тушения дорогостоящего оборудования или предметов, которые могут быть повреждены остатками других типов огнетушителей. Данное вещество хранится в жидком виде под давлением и испаряется при выгрузке для тушения пожаров."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":9625,"mass":165.36,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(F)(F)(Cl)Br","inchikey":"MEXUFEQDCXZEON-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"bromo-chloro-difluoromethane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9625","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.757,"y":-0.607,"z":0.0,"el":"Br"},{"x":-1.216,"y":-1.234,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.245,"y":0.876,"z":1.089,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.245,"y":0.876,"z":-1.089,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.051,"y":0.09,"z":0.0,"el":"C"}],"bonds":[[0,4,1],[1,4,1],[2,4,1],[3,4,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q419723","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bromochlorodifluoromethane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description",